  "synthesis": "According to company policy (HR-005), managers are held accountable for employee satisfaction in three key ways: their effectiveness scores from direct reports are factored into their own performance reviews; managers whose teams fall below the 25th percentile for two consecutive quarters must complete a 6-session People Manager Coaching programme over 12 weeks; and managers who fail to act on survey feedback within the action-planning window are escalated to their VP.\n\nThe data shows that satisfaction scores vary meaningfully across departments. Finance leads with an average score of 7.61, followed by Engineering at 7.20 and Customer Success at 6.97. HR (6.55) and Sales (6.53) sit at the bottom, with Sales being the least satisfied department overall. The data shows the full range spans from 6.53 to 7.61, meaning no department currently falls below 6.5, though HR and Sales managers may warrant closer monitoring under the policy's accountability framework given their relatively lower scores.",
  "refused": false,
  "refusal_reason": null
}

